{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver's own trace satisfies the POL-NS-02 proximity test outright: derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count is 39 consecutive qualifying fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius of the registered pickup pin at Blk 231 Serangoon Ave 3 (VEN-SERANGOON-AVE3), the driver's minimum distance to the pin is 0.0 m, and the single in-geofence run begins at 11:22:26 — the exact timestamp of the platform-recorded 'I'm Here' event in the trip record. Arrival under POL-NS-02, and therefore POL-NS-01 limb (b), is made out on the driver's evidence, and the radius is not in doubt: trip_record.pickup_zone_class is STANDARD, so the 50 m figure and the 25 m accuracy filter are the ones that apply.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02747", "EV-TRIP-02747"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The arrival marker is not false, so POL-NS-05 cannot be turned against the driver: at the 11:22:26 marker the trace already places him inside the pickup geofence — the qualifying run's first fix is 11:22:26 and his minimum distance to the pin is 0.0 m, far inside POL-NS-05's 300 m ceiling — and stationary, 0.0 kph being among his recorded speeds. There is accordingly neither a >300 m marker nor motion at or above 15 kph to void the waiting clock, the clock is not recomputed, and no false-arrival event falls to be recorded in the referrals under POL-NS-05(ii) or POL-NS-05(iii).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02747", "EV-TRIP-02747"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.first_ts",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The waiting requirement was exceeded, not missed. The driver held position inside the geofence continuously for 380 seconds, from 11:22:26 to 11:28:46 (derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec, 39 fixes), against the 180 seconds free waiting period in force for this trip under trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec; the derived shortfall is −200 seconds, a surplus. POL-NS-06 therefore licenses no refund on waiting-period-shortfall grounds, and because the whole dwell is served inside one continuous in-geofence interval, no accumulation of separate intervals under POL-NS-06(i) is needed and the MISSING traffic advisory at EV-ADVIS-02747-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) is immaterial to the driver's dwell.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02747", "EV-TRIP-02747", "EV-ADVIS-02747-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing in the driver's record supports the anti-farming concern or any escalation on his side. driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2, below the four-or-more limb of the POL-NS-07 check, and 2 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 138 is 0.0145, below the 0.08 rate limb, so the check does not trip on either limb and POL-NS-09(d) is not engaged against this driver. There is no pattern of fee harvesting to justify withholding the cancellation fee from him, and no counterparty-history trigger either: both disputes_with_counterparty_90d counters are 0, so POL-NS-09(c) is not engaged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02747", "EV-TRIP-02747"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The monetary exposure on any refund is bounded by what the ledger actually took. The only charge on this trip is the SGD 4.50 cancellation-fee line: total_charged is 4.50, the waiting_time_fee is 0.00, base fare, distance fare, time fare, surcharges and ERP are all 0.00, and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00. That line reconciles with the net figure in force for the trip, platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of SGD 4.50 (the ledger is permitted to show the net SGD 4.50 or the gross SGD 6.61 under POL-NS-08(d)), so no fare-integrity defect exists, no additional sum was charged, and nothing beyond the cancellation-fee line can be ordered.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02747", "EV-TRIP-02747"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fee_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I do not press a monetary win for the driver on the fee, and I say so plainly rather than stretch the record. The termination is recorded under cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE and the driver's own statement — 'Could not locate the rider so I cancelled' — confirms it; POL-NS-01 states in terms that DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE is the driver's own admission that he could not find the rider and does not satisfy limb (d). The fee is therefore not chargeable on this trip however clean the arrival and dwell facts are, and the only driver-side consequence the policy supports on these facts is the referral of the mis-selected reason code as a driver-education item, not any finding of fraud or fee-farming.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02747", "EV-CHAT-02747"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.5,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-01: driver-education item — the cancellation on trip TRP-02747 was recorded under reason code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE rather than a rider-failure code; the mis-selected reason code is to be recorded against driver DRV-09747."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider: your claim is upheld and the no-show cancellation fee of SGD 4.50 charged to you on trip TRP-02747 is refunded in full. The driver's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-02747, weight 1.0) places him inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at Blk 231 Serangoon Ave 3 from 11:22:26 to 11:28:46 — a continuous in-geofence dwell of 380 seconds (39 qualifying fixes) against the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip, so POL-NS-01 limbs (a), (b) and (c) are made out. Limb (d) is not. The trip was terminated with cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, and POL-NS-01(d) recognises only RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT; POL-NS-01 states in terms that DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE is the driver's own admission that he could not find the rider and does not satisfy limb (d). Because the four limbs are conjunctive and the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius, the clause directs a full refund of the cancellation fee with no driver compensation, the mis-selected code being recorded as a driver-education referral. The amount is taken from the fare ledger (EV-FARE-02747: total_charged SGD 4.50, cancellation_fee SGD 4.50, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd SGD 0.00) and reconciles with the net figure in force, platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of SGD 4.50. The rider's fallback exoneration under POL-NS-04 is also made out (locating message 'at the lift lobby' at 11:23:26, no driver reply within 120 seconds, rider track 13–19 m from the pin throughout), but it adds nothing to a refund already full. POL-NS-03 is not reached: the stationary fixes lie inside the 50 m radius, not outside it within 400 m, so no pin-ambiguity goodwill arises.\n\nTo the driver: your factual points are accepted. The arrival marker is not false — at 11:22:26 you were 0.0 m from the pin and stationary, so neither POL-NS-05 trigger fires and no false-arrival referral is made. Your dwell of 380 seconds exceeded the 180-second free waiting period, so POL-NS-06 licenses no refund and the missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-02747-01) is immaterial — it bears only on POL-NS-06(i), and your dwell was served in one continuous in-geofence interval. The fare ledger reconciles to the net figure, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect, and the anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d = 2, below the four-or-more limb, and 2/138 = 0.0145, below the 0.08 rate limb). But POL-NS-07 pays you only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and limb (d) fails: the obstacle is the reason code you selected, not your conduct on the ground. No driver compensation is therefore payable.\n\nNo POL-NS-09 escalation trigger fires. Nothing is impaired under POL-NS-08(a) to (d): the trace has 100% coverage, no sampling gap and 96 fixes; the arrival event at 11:22:26 matches the first qualifying fix exactly, so there is no clock skew; the chat log is complete at 2 messages with intact sequence numbering and matches trip_record.chat_message_count; and the cancellation-fee line equals the net figure. No admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence; both disputes_with_counterparty_90d counters are 0; rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0; and the anti-farming limbs are not met. The one discarded claim (see the audit record) rested on the missing advisory EV-ADVIS-02747-01 without naming its issue code and is in any event unnecessary. The deciding facts are carried by the trip record, GPS trace, chat log and fare ledger, all at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and confidence is 0.95, above the 0.70 floor. The monetary effect of SGD 4.50 is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so the refund executes automatically."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "EV-ADVIS-02747-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0), so no traffic advisory on record supports any kerb-restriction or closure excuse on this pickup road, and POL-NS-06(i) - which requires a traffic_advisory that is present and populated - is unavailable. The rider's claim does not rest on that artifact, so its absence can neither defeat the refund nor be turned against her.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02747-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.5,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-01: on trip TRP-02747 the driver terminated the trip under the mis-selected cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, a code that does not satisfy limb (d); recorded as a driver-education item."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider, your claim is upheld; Driver, the no-show fee cannot stand on this record. POL-NS-01 makes a no-show fee chargeable only where all four of its conditions hold together, and condition (d) requires the trip to have been terminated by the driver under RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT. The trip record EV-TRIP-02747 shows the trip cancelled by the driver at 11:28:47 under DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, and the driver's own statement ('Could not locate the rider so I cancelled') confirms it; POL-NS-01 states in terms that DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE is the driver's own admission that he could not find the rider and does not satisfy limb (d). With limb (d) failed the fee is not chargeable, and the surrounding facts put this squarely in the branch POL-NS-01 fixes for a wrong reason code: the GPS trace EV-GPS-02747 places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius continuously for 380 seconds (39 qualifying fixes, 11:22:26 to 11:28:46). So the cancellation fee of SGD 4.50 is refunded in full, no driver compensation is payable, and the mis-selected reason code goes into the referrals as a driver-education item. The rider independently succeeds under POL-NS-04: she sent a locating message ('at the lift lobby') at 11:23:26 inside the waiting window, the driver posted no reply within 120 seconds and placed no in-app call, and her device sat 13.1-19.1 m from the pin across all 65 fixes, well inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius; that clause also refunds the fee in full with no driver compensation. On the driver's claims: I accept the POL-NS-02 proximity test is met (39 consecutive in-radius fixes, minimum distance 0.0 m), that POL-NS-05 cannot mark the arrival false (the 11:22:26 marker already places him inside the geofence and stationary, far inside the 300 m ceiling and the 15 km/h threshold, so the waiting clock is not recomputed and no false-arrival referral arises), and that POL-NS-06 gives the rider no shortfall route - the 380-second dwell exceeds the 180-second free waiting period in trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec, the derived shortfall being -200 seconds, a surplus. Those findings do not save the fee, because limb (d) fails independently. I also accept there is no POL-NS-07 anti-farming pattern (no_show_terminations_30d is 2, below four, and 2/138 = 0.0145, below 0.08) and that the fare ledger reconciles with the SGD 4.50 net figure in force under POL-NS-08(d) - but POL-NS-07 pays the driver only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not, so the driver receives nothing; the driver conceded this correctly. The MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02747-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact here: the dwell is one continuous in-geofence interval, so no accumulation under POL-NS-06(i) is needed and its absence neither defeats nor supports the refund. The deciding facts rest on EV-TRIP-02747 and EV-GPS-02747, both COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, so confidence is not capped and stands at 0.9; no POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is engaged. The rider's claim that cites the missing advisory without naming its issue code is discarded as the referee recorded. The refund of SGD 4.50 is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold in POL-GEN-05 and executes automatically."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "EV-ADVIS-02747-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0), so no traffic advisory on record supports any kerb-restriction or closure excuse on this pickup road, and POL-NS-06(i) - which requires a traffic_advisory that is present and populated - is unavailable. The rider's claim does not rest on that artifact, so its absence can neither defeat the refund nor be turned against her.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02747-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
